        <mxCell id="card-legend-notes" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;Large dashed frame: infra perimeter · small: functional group&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;⚠ Gx&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;: docs and code disagree, see &quot;Gaps&quot;&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=10.5;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="3110" width="480" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-bg" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ea580c&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Background · control plane&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;A&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt; Argo CD syncs the EKS / GKE API (:443) with the argocd-manager token. CNP-112: cloud Applications retry forever.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;C&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;D&lt;/span&gt; The cloud secret operator logs in at auth/kubernetes-aws / -gcp on vault.3istor.com :443, with vault-secrets-operator-role and, for Alloy&amp;#39;s Loki password, observability-role.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;E&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;F&lt;/span&gt; The on-prem WireGuard pods initiate UDP 31820 to the cloud node (NodePort, pod 51820).&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;G&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;H&lt;/span&gt; Vault checks service-account tokens with TokenReview (SA vault-auth, auth-delegator). &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;I&lt;/span&gt; The hub secret operator reads Vault.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;X&lt;/span&gt; The operator opens ssh -D 1080 to pae-node-1. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;J&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;K&lt;/span&gt; Terraform and kubectl reach the cloud API through that SOCKS proxy, so the API sees the on-prem egress IP.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;L&lt;/span&gt; Terraform writes the cluster entry kvv2/argocd/clusters/&amp;lt;cloud&amp;gt; and the auth config into Vault. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;M&lt;/span&gt; It publishes &amp;lt;node IP&amp;gt;:31820 in the endpoint bucket. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;N&lt;/span&gt; The on-prem pod re-reads it when the last handshake is older than 180 s.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;O&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;P&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;Q&lt;/span&gt; The EKS kubeconfig in SSM, and the Terraform state in S3 and GCS.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;R&lt;/span&gt; Argo CD polls cnp-projects. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;S&lt;/span&gt; The CMP writes the registry record. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;U&lt;/span&gt; Image Updater reads GHCR tags and writes back to Git. &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;V&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;W&lt;/span&gt; Cloud nodes pull images from GHCR.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;Y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;Z&lt;/span&gt; The CMP reads pods, rollouts, scans and backups of cloud projects, with the token of the Argo CD Secret cluster-&amp;lt;cloud&amp;gt;. It refuses to call unless the cluster state is up.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="590" y="2700" width="820" height="460" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-allow" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#e11d48&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Who allows it&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Cloud API :443&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: only api_allowed_cidrs = the K3s egress 176.186.130.237/32. The operator gets there through pae-node-1, Argo CD and the CMP from the K3s pods. EKS: API access entry for the operator only.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;UDP 31820&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: EKS security group and GKE firewall, only from vpn_source_cidrs (the K3s egress).&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Relays 18080 / 18082 / 18083&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: NetworkPolicy onprem-apps in cnp-vpn on each cloud; on-prem, the VictoriaMetrics policies admit the wireguard pods. See multicloud-policies.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Vault&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: a Kubernetes auth mount per cloud (kubernetes-aws, kubernetes-gcp), kept across down.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Inbound to workloads&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;: none. Guardrails refuse LoadBalancer Services and Ingress; apps are reached only through outbound Cloudflare tunnels.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1440" y="2700" width="520" height="460" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-tunnel" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#d97706&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;What crosses the tunnel&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Cloud to on-prem, declared TCP relays only&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; (socat at each end): :18080 to vminsert :8480 (metrics), :18082 to loki-gateway :80 (logs), :18083 to vmselect :8481 (canary analysis).&lt;br&gt;• Clients: Alloy (ns observability) writes 18080 and 18082 with label cluster=aws|gcp; Argo Rollouts reads 18083.&lt;br&gt;• On-prem to cloud: :18081 to the cloud whoami, test only.&lt;br&gt;• Not through the tunnel: the CMP reads vmselect :8481 and the Loki gateway :80 directly, inside the hub.&lt;br&gt;• Argo CD &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;A&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt;, Vault &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;C&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;D&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;G&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;H&lt;/span&gt;, the CMP &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;Y&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;border:1px solid #0f172a;color:#0f172a;border-radius:3px;padding:0px 3px;font-weight:bold;&quot;&gt;Z&lt;/span&gt; and app traffic stay on the public Internet, limited by the allow-lists.&lt;br&gt;• Tunnels: 100.96.0.0/30 (AWS .1, on-prem .2) and 100.96.0.4/30 (GCP .5, on-prem .6).&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1990" y="2700" width="450" height="460" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="card-gaps" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#ea580c&quot;&gt;●&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Gaps between the plan and the code&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;line-height:1.6&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;G13&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Secret operator.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Ricoberger operator on hub and clouds: behaviour during a Vault outage is untested.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;G18&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Delete during a down.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; Cloud Applications retry forever with refresh (CNP-112); deleting one while its cluster is down hangs on the finalizer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;G7&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;CMP API auth.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; The backend verifies signature, issuer and expiry and the edge checks JWTs; the audience is still not checked.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;CMP egress.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; No proxy in kube_client: the CMP pod relies on the K3s node egress being 176.186.130.237. Inferred, not in code.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;GO1&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Relay auth.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; vminsert takes the writes with no credential: the cluster label is set by the client.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#c2410c&quot;&gt;GO2&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#0f172a&quot;&gt;Loki gateway.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/b&gt; No NetworkPolicy in front of it: basic auth is the only check.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#e2e8f0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=20;spacingTop=14;spacingRight=16;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#1e293b;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2470" y="2700" width="370" height="460" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
